  "question": {
    "text": "If the solution $y(x)$ of the given differential equation $\\left(\\mathrm{e}^y+1\\right) \\cos x \\mathrm{~d} x+\\mathrm{e}^y \\sin x \\mathrm{~d} y=0$ passes through the point $\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}, 0\\right)$, then the value of $\\mathrm{e}^{y\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)}$ is equal to_________",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\left(\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{y}}+1\\right) \\cos \\mathrm{x} \\mathrm{dx}+\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{y}} \\sin \\mathrm{x} d \\mathrm{y}=0 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{d}\\left(\\left(\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{y}}+1\\right) \\sin \\mathrm{x}\\right)=0 \\\\\n& \\left(\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{y}}+1\\right) \\sin \\mathrm{x}=\\mathrm{C}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />It passes through $\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}, 0\\right)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{c}=2$\nNow, $x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{y}}=3$",
    "image": null
  },
